## Prompt (copy/paste)

Execute the full DevOps lifecycle workflow for my new feature:

**Feature Name:** <<ADD YOUR IDEA NAME HERE>>
**Description:** <<ADD YOUR IDEA DESCRIPTION HERE>>
**Priority:** <<ADD A PRIORITY HERE ie High, Medium or Low>>

**Target Release Date:** <<ADD A TARGET RELEASE DATE HERE ie 2025-11-13>>

Please execute the following end-to-end workflow:

1. **Planning Phase:**
   - Create an Epic in Plan (EchoL application, PAYMENT project) with the feature name and description
   - Create initial user stories to break down the epic
   - Create a release event in Velocity with the target date
   - Track the work item in the value stream

2. **Development Phase:**
   - Create a feature branch in Control (use feature/[epic-id]-[feature-name] naming)
   - Move the work items to "Active" status
   - Create placeholder code files for the feature (suggest appropriate file structure)
   - Commit the initial implementation

3. **Code Review Phase:**
   - Create a pull request from the feature branch to main
   - Make appropriate edits to the code
   - Get my pending approvals list
   - Guide me through the review process
   - When you commit the code change, we use the format “workitem ID – <<message>>”

4. **Build & Test Phase:**
   - Monitor build data in Velocity after merge
   - List available test projects and execute relevant tests
   - Monitor test results and provide status
   - Download and analyze logs if there are failures

5. **Deployment Phase:**
   - List Deploy applications and environments
   - Create a snapshot of the component versions
   - Deploy to DEV environment
   - Monitor deployment status
   - Verify the deployment inventory

6. **Quality Gates Phase:**
   - Show the pipeline and gate status in Velocity
   - Compare DEV environment with TEST/STAGING
   - Deploy to STAGING environment
   - Execute acceptance tests

7. **Production Phase:**
   - Schedule or execute production deployment
   - Monitor production deployment status
   - Verify production inventory
   - Run smoke tests

8. **Post-Deployment Phase:**
   - Close work items in Plan
   - Update release event status in Velocity
   - Generate and display key metrics (lead time, deployment frequency, test results)
   - Suggest next steps and improvements

**Additional Parameters:**
- Component Name: [if known, otherwise suggest based on feature]
- Test Suite to Execute: [if known, otherwise suggest based on feature type]
- Deployment Process: [if known, otherwise use default]
- Skip any steps that require manual intervention but document what I need to do

Pause at each major phase to show me status and wait for my confirmation to proceed to the next phase.

